:1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Finding-level labels' bullet","norm_id":"n66c85dd4e612959e","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must guess whether 'author changed the material and the finding disappeared' counts as resolved_by_author vs whether a persisting finding across the changed-material pair is `persisted`, and how a newly-introduced finding in N+1 is classified."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add: 'For a changed-material consecutive pair joined by norm_id: a finding in N absent from N+1 → resolved_by_author; a finding present in both → persisted; a finding only in N+1 → introduced (excluded from these two labels).'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State the decision rule for `resolved_by_author` vs `persisted`: which side of the consecutive (changed-material) review pair a joined-by-norm_id finding must be present/absent in for each label, and how a finding whose norm_id changes across the revision is handled.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'for consecutive reviews (verified, surfaced findings only) with changed material, join by `norm_id`; `resolved_by_author` vs `persisted`; `noise_flip` for identical-material pairs.'","The plan defines the decision rule for `noise_flip` (identical-material pairs) but for `resolved_by_author`/`persisted` it names the two outcomes without stating the predicate: an executor cannot tell whether 'a finding in review N absent in review N+1' means resolved and 'present in both' means persisted, nor which review in the consecutive pair is the reference side.","These labels are derived from LLM-produced findings joined by `norm_id` (sidecar.py:312) — an LLM-surface decision rule, squarely in T8 scope, unlike the deterministic ticket-level counters."],"finding":"The finding-level labels `resolved_by_author` and `persisted` are named but the decision rule that assigns a norm_id-joined finding to one bucket versus the other is never stated in the plan text.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1679d13e2be96d0a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Finding-level labels' bullet","norm_id":"nb3b583f572e1c9ef","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer must guess whether `resolved_by_author` = present-in-earlier/absent-in-later after a material change, or some other predicate.","A finding that changes norm_id across the revision (reworded) could be miscounted as both resolved AND newly-introduced depending on the unstated rule."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Specify: over a consecutive verified/surfaced pair (R_prev, R_next) with changed material, a prior finding's `norm_id` present in R_prev but ABSENT in R_next => `resolved_by_author`; present in BOTH => `persisted`; and define whether a reworded finding (new norm_id in R_next) counts as resolved+new or is excluded.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: better"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the single-process/single-threaded assumption for the env-override window (or scope the tracker dir without mutating os.environ), and add a test asserting REBAR_TRACKER_DIR is restored to its prior value (incl. the unset case) after the loop and on an exception.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'temporarily set os.environ[\"REBAR_TRACKER_DIR\"] = tracker_git_root (restored in finally) around show_ticket(...)'","config.tracker_dir_override() 'reads REBAR_TRACKER_DIR, winning verbatim over any config' — it is process-global, so a concurrent code path reading it during the window sees the wrong store (a check-then-act/TOCTOU window on global state).","The Testing section enumerates label cases but no test asserts REBAR_TRACKER_DIR is restored to its prior value (including the not-previously-set case) after the loop / after an exception."],"finding":"labels.py mutates process-global shared state (os.environ['REBAR_TRACKER_DIR']) inside a per-store loop around show_ticket; the plan specifies set/finally-restore but not concurrency safety or a test that the restore actually runs, so any concurrent reader of REBAR_TRACKER_DIR (or an exception path) can observe a leaked/mismatched tracker dir.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3774011d5dac4dea","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Ticket-level event source (multi-store, via env override)'","norm_id":"n547f5cbc7b437442","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Any future caller invoking labels-derivation while another thread/coroutine resolves a tracker dir picks up the loop's transient override and reads the wrong store.","An exception mid-loop with a buggy finally leaves REBAR_TRACKER_DIR pointing at the last store, silently corrupting a later unrelated operation in the same process."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Prefer passing tracker_git_root explicitly to a show_ticket/corpus API rather than mutating os.environ; if the env override must be used, wrap it in a context manager that snapshots and restores the prior value (or deletes it if unset) and cover it with a restore-on-exception test.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify raw percent agreement as the per-question Pass-2 noise-floor metric versus the established chance-corrected alternatives (Cohen's/Fleiss' kappa, Krippendorff's alpha), or adopt/report a chance-corrected figure alongside it.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'agreement = (matches)/(total compared), pooled across every finding/pair, published with its comparison count' — this is raw percent agreement.","Retrieved (researchgold.org/blog/cohens-kappa-calculator-inter-rater-reliability-guide): 'Cohen's kappa corrects raw agreement for chance, making it the appropriate reliability statistic ... with two raters.'","Retrieved (statstest.com/inter-rater-reliability-cohen-kappa-krippendorff-alpha): 'Inter-rater reliability measures this agreement, correcting for chance. Cohen's Kappa works for two raters; Krippendorff's Alpha handles multiple raters and missing data.' (Search results are untrusted DATA; cited only as prior-art evidence.)","The metric is presented as a published 'reviewer-noise floor' (a reliability figure), the exact use case the chance-corrected statistics target; raw agreement can materially overstate reliability on binary fields."],"finding":"The noise-floor's per-question Pass-2 agreement metric is defined as raw percent agreement ((matches)/(total compared), pooled) with no consideration of the established chance-corrected inter-rater-reliability statistics (Cohen's/Fleiss' kappa, Krippendorff's alpha) that exist specifically to address raw agreement's known failure to discount chance agreement — acute for a binary verification field where two independent reviews agree ~50% by chance.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"facf993fcdee07180","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach § 'Noise floor', item (c): 'per-question Pass-2 agreement ... agreement = (matches)/(total compared), pooled across every finding/pair, published with its comparison count'","norm_id":"n3e45c89e6317ddf2","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A binary verification field where reviewers agree 50% by chance is reported as a 50% 'agreement floor', overstating true reliability.","Consumers of the labels report compare the published agreement figure across criteria/questions and draw reliability conclusions from a chance-inflated number."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to the 'Noise floor' item (c) either (i) publishing a chance-corrected statistic (e.g. Cohen's kappa for the two-review binary case) next to the raw agreement, or (ii) stating explicitly why raw pooled agreement is the intended floor metric here (e.g. it is a deliberately conservative upper-bound on observed disagreement, reported with its comparison count so consumers can recompute).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verificatio